
[38;5;231m⏺[39m Next: [1mthe shape of the calling interface.[0m You said other forms will need this, and since the storage backend is meant
  to be swappable, the API is the part that's actually expensive to get wrong — it's what every future call site is
  written against.

  - [1mGeneric core plus named helpers[0m — [38;5;153mtrack(eventName, data)[39m does the work; [38;5;153mtrackLogin(userId)[39m is a one-line wrapper
    over it. New forms can call [38;5;153mtrack[39m directly without editing the module, and the common cases still read clearly at
    the call site.
  - [1mGeneric only[0m — just [38;5;153mtrack(eventName, data)[39m. Smallest surface. Costs: every caller invents its own event name and
    field names, so the stored data drifts into inconsistency with nothing to catch a typo'd event name.
  - [1mNamed function per case[0m — [38;5;153mtrackLogin(userId)[39m, then [38;5;153mtrackSignup(...)[39m, and so on. Self-documenting and hard to misuse,
    but every new form means editing the tracker, which is the opposite of "other forms will need it later."

  [1mRecommendation: generic core plus named helpers.[0m One extra function buys you readable call sites now and a module
  nobody has to modify to add a form later.

